# What the robot works on from now on, as natural-language prompts at the GUIDE-EX layers:
#   task    -- one complete job, e.g. "Put the red cube on the blue cube."; it is every
#              following frame's LeRobot task.
#   subtask -- a part of the task, e.g. "Pick up the red cube."; it is recorded as
#              LeRobot's `subtask` language style.
# Both are applied at once, so no frame pairs a new task with the last task's subtask; an
# empty field leaves its level as it is. Every frame the scene records after this carries
# them, until the next prompt of the same level or the end of the episode. The
# procedure-level prompt ("Stack the cubes.") is drawn by the scene's randomization and
# recorded as GUIDE's `procedure` language style.
int32 id
string task
string subtask
---
bool success
string message
